{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.116.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin (`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a different one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes libcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`, to `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc3-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc3-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11856-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11856 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Successfully using libcurl to do a transfer to a specific HTTP origin (`hostA`) with **Digest** authentication and then changing the origin to a different one (`hostB`) for a second transfer, reusing the same handle, makes libcurl wrongly pass on the  `Authorization:` header field meant for `hostA`, to `hostB`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc3-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11856**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc3-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-11856](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11856)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8925-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8925 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The curl logic that works with SASL authentication could end up cleaning up the GSASL context *twice* without clearing the pointer in between, making it `free()` the same pointer twice."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8925\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8925](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8925**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8925](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8925-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8925 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The curl logic that works with SASL authentication could end up cleaning up the GSASL context *twice* without clearing the pointer in between, making it `free()` the same pointer twice."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8925\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8925](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8925**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8925](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8925)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9079-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9079 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl had a flaw that when instructed to clear proxy authentication credentials which made it not do so, leaving the old credentials around to get used for subsequent transfers that should not know nor use them."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9079-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9079 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl had a flaw that when instructed to clear proxy authentication credentials which made it not do so, leaving the old credentials around to get used for subsequent transfers that should not know nor use them."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8924-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8924 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in curl’s cookie parsing logic allows a malicious HTTP server to set 'super cookies' that bypass the Public Suffix List check. This enables an attacker-controlled origin to inject cookies that curl subsequently scopes and transmits to unrelated third-party domains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8924\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8924](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8924**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8924](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8924-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8924 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in curl’s cookie parsing logic allows a malicious HTTP server to set 'super cookies' that bypass the Public Suffix List check. This enables an attacker-controlled origin to inject cookies that curl subsequently scopes and transmits to unrelated third-party domains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8924\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8924](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8924**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8924](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8924)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-10536 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application configures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and finally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final cleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure that was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-10536-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-10536 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability exists in libcurl when an application configures an HTTP/2 stream-dependency tree via `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS` or `CURLOPT_STREAM_DEPENDS_E`, subsequently invokes `curl_easy_reset()`, and finally terminates the handle with `curl_easy_cleanup()`. During this final cleanup phase, libcurl attempts to access and modify an internal structure that was already freed during the reset operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-10536**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-10536](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-10536)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11352-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11352 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue in curl’s QUIC UDP receive function allows a malicious HTTP/3 server to trigger a remote denial of service against a curl or libcurl client. Because the helper function discards zero-length UDP datagrams before counting them toward the per-call packet budget, a connected QUIC peer can continuously stream empty datagrams to indefinitely stall the client."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11352\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-11352](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11352**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-11352](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11352-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11352 high vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue in curl’s QUIC UDP receive function allows a malicious HTTP/3 server to trigger a remote denial of service against a curl or libcurl client. Because the helper function discards zero-length UDP datagrams before counting them toward the per-call packet budget, a connected QUIC peer can continuously stream empty datagrams to indefinitely stall the client."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11352\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-11352](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11352**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-11352](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11352)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8927-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8927 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reusing a libcurl handle for sequential transfers driven by environment-variable proxy configuration, libcurl fails to clear the proxy authentication state between requests. Specifically, if the initial transfer authenticates against `proxyA` using Digest auth, a subsequent transfer routed through `proxyB` erroneously leaks the `Proxy-Authorization:` header intended solely for `proxyA`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8927-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8927 critical vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When reusing a libcurl handle for sequential transfers driven by environment-variable proxy configuration, libcurl fails to clear the proxy authentication state between requests. Specifically, if the initial transfer authenticates against `proxyA` using Digest auth, a subsequent transfer routed through `proxyB` erroneously leaks the `Proxy-Authorization:` header intended solely for `proxyA`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-8927**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4t64  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-8927](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8927)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
