            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41992-gzip",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41992 high vulnerability for gzip package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU gzip contains a global buffer overflow vulnerability in the LZH decompression logic caused by improper reuse of shared global state between different decompression formats within a single execution. GNU gzip maintains a global array that is shared across the LZ77, LZW, and LZH decompression routines and is not reinitialized between files processed in the same invocation. By decompressing a specially crafted LZW file followed by a specially crafted LZH file in a single gzip -d command, an attacker can poison the shared global state and subsequently trigger an out‑of‑bounds read in the LZH decoder. The LZH decompression logic follows stale values left in the shared array, causing reads past the end of the allocated global buffer.  This issue has been fixed in the commit 63dbf6b3b9e6e781df1a6a64e609b10e23969681"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992\nSeverity: high\nPackage: gzip\nVersion: 1.13-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | gzip  | 1.13-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/gzip@1.13-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-66035-libssh2-1t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-66035 high vulnerability for libssh2-1t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit 42e33d8, contains a pre-authentication heap buffer overflow vulnerability that allows a malicious SSH server to corrupt heap metadata in any connecting client by sending a packet with a packet_length smaller than the cipher's block size during Encrypt-then-MAC cipher negotiation. In the fullpacket() function in src/transport.c, the ETM path allocates a buffer of packet_length bytes but copies blocksize minus one bytes via memcpy, causing an overflow that on 32-bit glibc writes attacker-controlled bytes into an adjacent chunk's SIZE field, enabling tcache bin confusion, overlapping live objects, and function pointer overwrite during the session handshake before authentication."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66035",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-66035\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1t64\nVersion: 1.11.1-4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-66035](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66035)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-66035**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1t64  | 1.11.1-4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-66035](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66035)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1t64@1.11.1-4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8286-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8286 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability exists where a new transfer that uses STARTTLS to upgrade the connection might reuse an existing live connection even though the TLS configuration mismatches so it should not."
