            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-66032-libssh2-1t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-66032 high vulnerability for libssh2-1t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit 5e47761, contains a double-free vulnerability in the sftp_open() function in src/sftp.c that allows a malicious SSH server to corrupt the heap of any authenticated client opening an SFTP session. When a server responds to SSH_FXP_OPEN with SSH_FXP_STATUS containing FX_OK, the response data buffer is freed, and if a subsequent sftp_packet_require() call returns a specific error such as LIBSSH2_ERROR_CHANNEL_PACKET_EXCEEDED, the same pointer is freed a second time, enabling tcache dup conditions on glibc systems that allow overlapping allocations and function pointer overwrites."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66032",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-66032\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1t64\nVersion: 1.11.1-4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-66032](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66032)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-66032**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1t64  | 1.11.1-4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-66032](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66032)  |\n"
              },
