            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-66034-libssh2-1t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-66034 high vulnerability for libssh2-1t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit a13bb6c, contains a missing bounds check vulnerability that allows a malicious SSH server to trigger an arbitrary-length heap out-of-bounds read and a free of an uninitialized pointer via the publickey subsystem. In libssh2_publickey_list_fetch(), the version 1 response parser reads a server-controlled comment_len value and advances the parse pointer without verifying sufficient bytes remain in the buffer, causing the out-of-bounds read to leak heap pointers from adjacent allocations defeating ASLR, followed by heap allocator state corruption when the error cleanup path frees an uninitialized pointer from a non-zeroed realloc() region."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1t64\nVersion: 1.11.1-4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1t64  | 1.11.1-4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1t64@1.11.1-4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-7017-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-7017 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP::Tiny versions before 0.095 for Perl forward credential headers to cross-origin redirect targets.  When the server returns a 3xx redirect, `_maybe_redirect` follows the `Location:` header and `_prepare_headers_and_cb` re-merges the caller's `headers` argument into the new request, without checking whether the redirect target shares an origin with the original URL. Caller-supplied `Authorization`, `Cookie` and `Proxy-Authorization` headers are therefore re-sent to whatever host the redirect names, across scheme, host or port boundaries, and including `https` to `http` downgrades that expose them in plaintext on the wire.  The HTTP::Tiny POD note that \"Authorization headers will not be included in a redirected request\" applied only to the URL-userinfo Basic-auth path, not to headers passed explicitly by the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-8\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-7017](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-7017**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-8  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-7017](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-7017)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.40.1-8?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8458-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8458 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl might in some circumstances reuse the wrong connection when asked to do Negotiate-authenticated ones, even when they are set to use different 'services'.  libcurl features a pool of recent connections so that subsequent requests can reuse an existing connection to avoid overhead.  When reusing a connection a range of criteria must be met. Due to a logical error in the code, a request that was issued by an application could wrongfully reuse an existing connection to the same server that was authenticated using different services."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8458",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8458\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-8458](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8458)",
