            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9547-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9547 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When a libcurl-based application performs transfers via `SCP://` or `SFTP://` and utilizes the `CURLOPT_SSH_KEYFUNCTION` callback, it may silently accept an untrusted server. This vulnerability occurs when a server presents a host key type that does not match the specific key type already recorded for that host in the `known_hosts` file. Instead of rejecting the mismatch, the callback mechanism fails to properly enforce the restriction, allowing the connection to succeed without warning and risking a potential man-in-the-middle attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9547",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9547\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.20.0-5\nFix Version: 8.21.0~rc2-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-9547](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9547)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9547**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.20.0-5  | 8.21.0~rc2-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-9547](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9547)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.20.0-5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.4"
              }
            },
